Tidy← {
  ⍝ Tidy
  ⍝ Try to align comments nicely in dfn or tradfn source (and code files generally).
  ⍝ ---------
  ⍝ Syntax:
  ⍝ @cvv← [opts] ∇ source
  ⍝   source: [sourceDoc | sourceFnOp | sourceFi]
  ⍝   opts:   (tab: 65 ⋄ inc: 5  ⋄ min: 20  ⋄ pairs: 1 ⋄ fi: 0 )
  ⍝ ------
  ⍝ source: 
  ⍝   sourceDoc:   the source document to format.   @cvv: a char vector of vectors.
  ⍝   sourceFnOp:  the name of a function or operator with the code to format, with (fi:0).  @cv: a char vector.
  ⍝   sourceFi:    the name of a file with the code to format, with (fi:1). @cv: a char vector, (fi: 1).
  ⍝ opts: 
  ⍝   tab:   column in which to put comments if possible; 
  ⍝          defaults to 60.
  ⍝      Format:
  ⍝        Mode       num style    Example     Meaning (rounded)
  ⍝        ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ⍝        absolute    int         '15', 20    tab← num 
  ⍝        relative    '-digits'   '-10'       tab← lll - num 
  ⍝        relative    '+digits'   '+10'       tab← lll + num
  ⍝        relative    '×digits'   '×0.1'      tab← lll × num 
  ⍝      where
  ⍝        lll:  the length of the longest line of ⍵, 
  ⍝              excluding spaces and comments.
  ⍝   inc:   If text extends to <tab> or beryond, place comments multiples of <inc>
  ⍝          to the right of position <tab>
  ⍝   min:   Keep any comments before column <min> where they are.
  ⍝   fi:    If 1 and ⍵ has depth ≤1, treats ⍵ as the name of a file to update in place (see below).
  ⍝          Otherwise, a char vector right arg is treated as a fn or operator name.
  ⍝   pairs: If 1, will recognize pairs of comments on line line, 
  ⍝            - the first a left-side comment and
  ⍝            - the other aligned with the right-hand side comments. 
  ⍝          - The two must be have at least 5 blanks in between. 
  ⍝          If 0, only one comment is allowed.
  ⍝ Example of pairs: 
  ⍝⍝   ⍝ this is the left-side comment                      ⍝ And this is the right-side comment
  ⍝⍝                                             ⍝ This is only a right-side comment
  ⍝
  ⍝ Description
  ⍝ 1. If source is a char vector of vectors, it is treated as multiline APL code (a fn, op, etc.)
  ⍝    a.  Return the source with comments aligned per options.
  ⍝    b.  The object is NOT refixed-- that's up to you.
  ⍝ 2. If source is a char. vector, and...
  ⍝    a.  if fi is 0,
  ⍝        - ⍵ refers to the name of a visible function;
  ⍝        - its source representation (verbatim if possible) is formatted and...
  ⍝          - returned as a shy value;
  ⍝    b.  if fi is 1,
  ⍝        - ⍵ refers to a file, which is read;
  ⍝        - its source is formatted and...
  ⍝          - rewritten to the file (in place) and
  ⍝          - returned as a shy value.
  ⍝
  11 22:: ⎕SIGNAL⊂⎕DMX.('EN'EN ⋄ 'Message'Message)
    ⍝ Initialise
      ⎕IO ⎕ML← 0 1
      ⍺← ()
    ⍝ Variable defs  
      fnOpÊ← ⊂( 'EN' 11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown function or operator' )
      optÊ←  ⊂( 'EN' 11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown option(s)' )
      tabÊ←  ⊂( 'EN' 11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Invalid tab value' )
      o← (                                  ⍝ Default options
        tab: 60 ⋄ inc: 5 ⋄ min: 20 ⋄ pairs: 1 ⋄ fi: 0  
      ) 
    ⍝ Function defs  
      ∆Tidy← ∇                              ⍝ this function ("me")
      FOF← o∘{                              ⍝ Is it an in-core fn/op or a file
        ~⍺.fi: _← ⍺{                        ⍝ File with code of any type
            ~⍵ ⎕NC⍛∊ 3 4: ⎕SIGNAL fnOpÊ
              ⍺ ∆Tidy 62 ⎕ATX ⍵             ⍝ Get and process. Don't re-fix 
        }⍵
            ⍺.fi← 0                         ⍝ In-core function
            ll← ⍺ ∆Tidy ⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1          ⍝ Get and process
        1: _← ll⊣ ll⊂⍛⎕NPUT ⍵ 1             ⍝ Rewrite in place 
      }
      AL← {                                 ⍝ Align line
            ( t i ) p← ⍺.(tab inc) ⍵ 
         p≤t: ''⍴⍨ 1⌈ ¯1+ t- p              ⍝ Always add at least 1 space
              ''⍴⍨ 1⌈ ¯1+ i| p- t           ⍝ -- Ditto --
      }
      AT← {                                 ⍝ Generate Absolute Tab
        0=⊃0⍴⍺: ⍺ ⋄ f← ⊃⍺ 
          in out← ↓⍉↑(       
            '''[^'']*''' '&'
            '\h*⍝.*$'    ''
            '\h*$'       ''
          )
          WL← ⌈/≢¨⍤(in ⎕R out)             ⍝ Length of Widest Line 
          V← ⊃∘⌽∘⎕VFI
        '+-×'∊⍨ f: (WL ⍵) (⍎f) V 1↓⍺ ⋄ V ⍺ 
      }
      TB← { +/∧\' '= ⌽⍵ }                   ⍝ Trailing blanks
      LB← { +/∧\' '=  ⍵ }                   ⍝ Leading blanks 
      RF← {                                 ⍝ Regex Field
        ⍺.Lengths[⍵]↑ ⍺.Offsets[⍵]↓ ⍺.Block 
      } 

⍝ Execute Main 
      ×≢⊃~/(⍺ o).⎕NL ¯2: ⎕SIGNAL optÊ       ⍝ Only valid options?
      _← o ⎕NS ⍺                            ⍝ Add user options
  1≥≡⍵: FOF ,⍵                              ⍝ If ⍵ is CV, see of a fn (fi:0) or a file (fi:1)?
⍝ Calculate the absolute tab, as needed
      o.tab← o.tab AT ⍵
    ⍝ Prepare to pattern match
      pos← 0                                ⍝ pos:     Our position on this line.
      noCod← 1                              ⍝ noCod:   Just code on the line of ⍵?
      stI cdI _ lcI cmI spI← ⍳≢pats← (
          '^'                               ⍝ start    (of line)
          '''[^'']*''|[^⍝''\h]+'            ⍝ code     (fragments)
          o.pairs⊃ (                        ⍝ double comments
            '(*F)'                          ⍝ nop pattern, i.e. ignore
            '^(\h{,', (⍕0⌈¯1+o.min ), '}⍝[^⍝]*)\h{5,}(⍝.*)$'
          )          
          '\h*⍝⍝.*$'                        ⍝ literal comment (don't format)
          '\h*⍝.*$'                         ⍝ comment  (w/ preceding spaces)
          '\h+'                             ⍝ spaces   (not before comment)
      )
    ⍝ Pattern matching scan
      pats ⎕R{  
          m← ⍵.Match
          Case← ⍵.PatternNum∘=
        Case stI: m⊣ pos⊢← 0  ⊣ noCod⊢← 1   ⍝ Start of line
        Case cdI: m⊣ pos+← ≢m ⊣ noCod⊢← 0   ⍝ Code found
        Case lcI: m⊣ pos+← ≢m               ⍝ literal comment '⍝⍝'
        Case spI: m⊣ pos+← ≢m               ⍝ Spaces (not foll by comment)
      ⍝ Comment patterns, cmI and double comment pattern
          nsp← LB m  
        noCod∧ o.min> pos+ nsp: {           ⍝ If LHS comment...
          Case cmI: m                       ⍝ ... If std comment, return w/ leading spaces
 ⍝ ... If "double" comment, ...                                    
            cm1 cm2← ⍵ RF¨ 1 2              ⍝ ... get LHS and RHS comments
            cm1↓⍨← -TB cm1                  ⍝ ... Remove trail. blanks from LHS...
            pad← o AL pos+ ≢cm1             ⍝ ... align "2nd" comment on RHS
            cm1, pad, cm2                   ⍝ Return
        } ⍵                                            
          m↓⍨← nsp                          ⍝ If RHS comment 
          m,⍨  o AL pos                     ⍝ ... align at a valid tab stop.
      }⊣⍵
}
